---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About">
  <div class="wrap page-body">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Intelligence for South African entrepreneurs.</h1>
    <p>
      Straatpreneur is a weekly online intelligence magazine for South African entrepreneurs.
      The name fuses straat, the street, with entrepreneur: street-smart, self-made, hustle with
      substance. We track where the money moves: funding opportunities, public procurement flows,
      government and private capital, entrepreneurship competitions, and the strategies real
      founders use to raise it. Think of it as a weekly briefing on SA SMME money.
    </p>
    <h2>The six sections</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>The Ledger</strong> covers public procurement: where government money moved,
      notable tender awards, and sector patterns. <strong>Capital</strong> tracks funding: what
      is open, what closed, what changed at the agencies, the DFIs, and the banks.
      <strong>Winners</strong> profiles real, named entrepreneurs who won real competitions or
      secured real funding. <strong>The Playbook</strong> is evergreen strategy: how to raise,
      how to pitch, how to get bid-ready. <strong>The Blueprint</strong> puts one researched
      business idea on the table each edition: the market gap, what it takes to start, and the
      numbers. <strong>The Wire</strong> is the briefs column: deadlines opening and closing in
      the next 30 days.
    </p>
    <h2>How we work</h2>
    <p>
      Straatpreneur is researched with AI and edited by humans. Every figure is sourced. Every
      factual claim in every article, funding amounts, deadlines, winner names, programme rules,
      tender values, is checked against a public source before publication, and every factual
      article lists its sources at the bottom with the date we accessed them.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we cannot verify a story, we do not run it. We never invent entrepreneurs, quotes, or
      success stories: winner profiles only cover real, publicly reported winners of real
      competitions, with a source link. Our artwork is original illustration and charts built
      from verified data, never stock photography of people.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If you spot an error, tell us and we will fix it and note the correction. Accuracy is the
      whole product.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
